{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 21,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Job answered and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hear diligently my speech;\nAnd let this be your consolations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Suffer me, and I also will speak;\nAnd after that I have spoken, mock on.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As for me, is my complaint to man?\nAnd why should I not be impatient?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Mark me, and be astonished,\nAnd lay your hand upon your mouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Even when I remember I am troubled,\nAnd horror taketh hold on my flesh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore do the wicked live,\nBecome old, yea, wax mighty in power?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Their seed is established with them in their sight,\nAnd their offspring before their eyes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Their houses are safe from fear,\nNeither is the rod of God upon them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Their bull gendereth, and faileth not;\nTheir cow calveth, and casteth not her calf.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They send forth their little ones like a flock,\nAnd their children dance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They sing to the timbrel and harp,\nAnd rejoice at the sound of the pipe.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They spend their days in prosperity,\nAnd in a moment they go down to Sheol.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they say unto God, Depart from us;\nFor we desire not the knowledge of thy ways.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What is the Almighty, that we should serve him?\nAnd what profit should we have, if we pray unto him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lo, their prosperity is not in their hand:\nThe counsel of the wicked is far from me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How oft is it that the lamp of the wicked is put out?\nThat their calamity cometh upon them?\nThat ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "God",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " distributeth sorrows in his anger?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That they are as stubble before the wind,\nAnd as chaff that the storm carrieth away?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye say",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", God layeth up his iniquity for his children.\nLet him recompense it unto himself, that he may know it:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let his own eyes see his destruction,\nAnd let him drink of the wrath of the Almighty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For what careth he for his house after him,\nWhen the number of his months is cut off?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall any teach God knowledge,\nSeeing he judgeth those that are high?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "One dieth in his full strength,\nBeing wholly at ease and quiet:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His pails are full of milk,\nAnd the marrow of his bones is moistened.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And another dieth in bitterness of soul,\nAnd never tasteth of good.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They lie down alike in the dust,\nAnd the worm covereth them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, I know your thoughts,\nAnd the devices wherewith ye would wrong me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For ye say, Where is the house of the prince?\nAnd where is the tent wherein the wicked dwelt?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Have ye not asked wayfaring men?\nAnd do ye not know their evidences,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That the evil man is reserved to the day of calamity?\nThat they are led forth to the day of wrath?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who shall declare his way to his face?\nAnd who shall repay him what he hath done?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet shall he be borne to the grave,\nAnd men shall keep watch over the tomb.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The clods of the valley shall be sweet unto him,\nAnd all men shall draw after him,\nAs there were innumerable before him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.21.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.21.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How then comfort ye me in vain,\nSeeing in your answers there remaineth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "only",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " falsehood?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
